##Harmonised Landsat and Sentinel data extraction
We are extracting Harmonised Landsat and Sentinel evi data for trial sites with mortality date 2016 onwards (when HLS started collection data consistently). We will then compare with MODIS to assess whether the better spatial resolution can improve forest mortality detection.

Possible outcomes:
1. HLS decline starts earlier than MODIS = very strong result
2. Same timing of decline but larger magnitude for HLS
3. Spatial comparison - compare imagery pre and post mortality. HLS change in NDVI will reveal mortality patterns often hidden in MODIS pixel.
4. Formal (statistical) evaluation (for all sites): Calculate for each mortality event:
(i) Pre-event mean
(ii) Post event mean
(iii) % decline
For MODIS NDVI, HLS NDVI and HLS EVI
Compare distributions > median decline e.g. MODIS -12%, HLS -24%, EVI -31%

